<title>USA: Peabody sees power marketing move by mid-year.</title>
<headline>Peabody sees power marketing move by mid-year.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peabody Holding Co Inc expects to complete the acquisition of a U.S. power marketing company during the first half of the year, chief executive Irl Engelhardt said Monday.</p>
<p>Earlier, he told analysts power trading is one of the new ways Peabody is looking at to restructure its long term U.S. coal contracts. Peabody is a subsidiary of Energy Group Plc, which Hanson Plc expects to spin off this month.</p>
<p>The information statement for the planned spin-off discloses the talks with the power marketer, which Engelhardt declined to identify. ((-- Jim Brumm 212-859-1710.))</p>
